From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:39:36 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 199/202] Meridian: updates download only the difference from
 the installed version

A release may carry Meridian-<from>-to-<version>-mac-<arch>.delta (listed in
its signed SHA256SUMS): manifest.json and zstd patches against the old files.
The updater downloads the one for its version, builds the new app next to the
installed one (unchanged files cloned, every file checked against the
manifest's checksum, the installed files against the ones the delta was made
from), then checks it as it checks a full download. Anything wrong (no delta,
a changed installation, a broken patch, a failed download): the whole zip, as
before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
